<title>EGYPT: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>EGYPT GOVERNMENT LIST (970708)</p>
<p>President (Sworn in 12 Oct 93 for a third</p>
<p>    six-year term)................Hosni MUBARAK</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p>NATIONAL DEMOCRATIC PARTY (NDP) GOVERNMENT (Formed 3 Jan 96)</p>
<p>Prime Minister...Kamal GANZOURI</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Planning &amp; International Cooperation)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.............Youssef WALI</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Agriculture &amp; Land Reclamation)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Land Reclamation...See Deputy PM</p>
<p> Cabinet Affairs...Talaat HAMMAD</p>
<p> Culture............Farouk HOSNI</p>
<p> Defence..Field Marshal Mohamed Hussein TANTAWI</p>
<p> Economy...Youssef BOUTROS-GHALI</p>
<p> Education..............Hussein Kamel BAHAEDDIN</p>
<p> Electricity &amp; Energy...............Maher ABAZA</p>
<p> Finance.....Mohieddin el-GHARIB</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs......Amr MOUSSA</p>
<p> Health &amp; Population..............Ismail SALLAM</p>
<p> Higher Education..Moufid SHEHAB</p>
<p> (Also minister of state for scientific research)</p>
<p> Housing, New Communities.............Mohamed Ibrahim SOLEIMAN</p>
<p> Industry..........Soleiman REDA</p>
<p> Information....Safwat el-SHERIF</p>
<p> Interior.........Hassan el-ALFI</p>
<p> Justice......Farouk SEIFUL-NASR</p>
<p> Manpower &amp; Employment...........Ahmed el-AMAWI</p>
<p> Oil..............Hamdi el-BANBI</p>
<p> Planning &amp; International Cooperation.......See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Public Enterprise....Atef OBEID</p>
<p> Public Works &amp; Water Resources...............Mahmoud Abu ZAID</p>
<p> Religious Endowments.....Mahmoud Hamdi ZAKZOUK</p>
<p> Rural Development...............Mahmoud SHERIF</p>
<p> Social Affairs &amp; Social Insurance...........Mervat el-TELLAWI</p>
<p> Supply &amp; Trade.....Ahmed GUEILY</p>
<p> Tourism......Mamdouh el-BELTAGI</p>
<p> Transport, Communications, Civil Aviation...Soleiman METWALLI</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OF STATE:</p>
<p> Administrative Development (Civil Service</p>
<p>    Reform)...............Mohamed Zaki ABU AMER</p>
<p> Environmental Affairs.......Nadia Makram OBEID</p>
<p> Military Production........Mohamed el-GHAMRAWI</p>
<p> People's Assembly &amp; Shura Assembly............Kamal el-SHAZLI</p>
<p> Planning &amp; International Cooperation..........Zafer el-BISHRI</p>
<p> Scientific Research..See Minister of Education</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p> Parliament Speaker................Fathi SOROUR</p>
<p>				  - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor............Ismail HASSAN</p>
